        "intuition": "This loss applies a Huber-like smoothing to the adaptive cost_gap term to reduce abrupt gradient changes and enhance stability, while preserving symmetric margins and adaptive scaling with cost_gap. It balances gradient magnitudes by clamping and normalizing to improve training robustness.",
        "pseudocode": "margin = log_prob_w - log_prob_l\nrev_margin = log_prob_l - log_prob_w\nsym_margin = 0.5 * (margin - rev_margin)  # symmetrized margin\nscale = 0.1 * (mean(abs(cost_gap)) + 1e-6)\n# Huber smoothing on cost_gap to limit extremes\ndelta = 1.0\nabs_cg = abs(cost_gap)\nadaptive_cost = where(abs_cg < delta, cost_gap, delta * (cost_gap / (abs_cg + eps)))\nadaptive_term = scale * adaptive_cost\nweighted_margin = alpha * sym_margin - adaptive_term + bias\nclipped_margin = clamp(weighted_margin, -10, 10)\nloss_per_pair = -logsigmoid(clipped_margin)\nweighted_loss = loss_per_pair * weight\nloss = sum(weighted_loss) / (sum(weight) + eps)",
